title: the_meeting
speaker: dm
---
<<map the_meeting>>
You've been traveling for several days now. You don't have anywhere in particular you're trying to go, just enjoying the countryside. #line:start
As the day wanes, you see a bridge up the road a little ways. It's not a very large bridge and spans what is either a large creek or a small river, you're not sure. #line:the_meeting_1
Shortly before the bridge, you hear hushed voices off in the woods. You pause for a moment to listen, but can't quite make out the words. #line:the_meeting_2
You step off the road towards the voices and come to a forest clearing where several people have gathered. From the clothes they wear they're mostly villagers and farmers, and not very prosperous ones. #line:the_meeting_3
...comes down and demands I make a new massive roasting spit. Then takes it with no payment. Says it's for the new taxes. #line:the_meeting_4 #speaker:barnaby
Probably for my prized sow. He took her too. Didn't give me a choice. #line:the_meeting_5 #speaker:tobias
Little Tobias the Younger told me Lord Pissledown took one of the pigs, but he didn't tell me it was Her Royal Hoggness! The nerve! #line:the_meeting_6 #speaker:mabel
Only a year since the lordling came here and already the taxes... Oi, who're you? #line:the_meeting_7 #speaker:barnaby
The man in the blacksmith's apron turns to you, waiting for an answer. #line:the_meeting_8
Barnaby, leave off. Can't you see this is just a traveler. #line:the_meeting_9 #speaker:mabel
Probably an adventurer. #line:the_meeting_10 #speaker:tobias
Or one of his lordship's spies. #line:the_meeting_11 #speaker:barnaby
Barnaby glares at you, still waiting for an answer. #line:the_meeting_12
<<jump meeting_answer>>
===
title: meeting_answer
speaker: dm
---
-> I'm just traveling. Who's Lord Pissledown? #line:the_meeting_13
    <<set $clearing_stayed to true>>
    <<jump meeting_explained>>
-> I'm an adventurer. Sounds like you could use some help. #line:the_meeting_14
    <<set $clearing_stayed to true>>
    <<jump meeting_explained>>
-> Just a traveler. I'll be on my way now. #line:the_meeting_15
    <<jump meeting_leave>>
===
title: meeting_leave
speaker: dm
---
Ignore the villagers and continue? #line:meeting_leave_ask
-> Yes, continue down the road. #line:meeting_leave_yes
    <<set $clearing_left to true>>
    You leave the villagers behind and head down the road to the nearest village in the darkening twilight. #line:meeting_leave_go
    <<jump briarwood_arrival>>
-> No, stay and answer them. #line:meeting_leave_no
    <<jump meeting_answer>>
===
title: meeting_explained
speaker: dm
---
Lord Percival Thistledown— #line:feast_note_1_a_or_b_1 #speaker:mabel
Pompous jerk. #line:feast_note_1_a_or_b_2 #speaker:tobias
Tobias! #line:feast_note_1_a_or_b_3 #speaker:barnaby
What? He is. #line:feast_note_1_a_or_b_4 #speaker:tobias
My students call him Petty Percy Pissledown. #line:feast_note_1_a_or_b_5 #speaker:mabel
You let them?! What if someone tells his lordship? #line:meeting_let_them #speaker:barnaby
Of course I can't condone it. I just pretend not to hear it. #line:meeting_pretend #speaker:mabel
And hide the laugh? #line:meeting_hide_laugh #speaker:tobias
Well, you have to appreciate the alliteration. Hehehe. #line:meeting_alliteration #speaker:mabel
No, you don't have to appreciate it. You don't want his lordship bringing you up on charges for that! #line:meeting_charges #speaker:barnaby
Charges? #line:meeting_charges_q #speaker:tobias
Yeah, alliteration is when you get in trouble for something even if you haven't done it. #line:meeting_barnaby_wrong #speaker:barnaby
You're thinking of allegation, Barnaby. Alliteration is just when several words start with the same sound. #line:meeting_allegation #speaker:mabel
Whatever, still not worth the risk. #line:meeting_not_worth #speaker:barnaby
As Barnaby, Mabel, and Tobias argue their way to an explanation, the sun sets and the clearing darkens. Mabel lights a lantern so you can still see the clearing. #line:meeting_lantern
You eventually get the idea that Lord Percival Thistledown, aka Lord Pissledown, became lord of a small cluster of villages almost a year ago. He has raised taxes three times already this year. #line:meeting_the_idea
He decided to hold a lavish celebration later this month. To make the celebration as memorable as possible, he's raised taxes for a fourth time. #line:meeting_fourth_time
The villagers never ask for help. They seem to be at a loss for what can be done about the situation. #line:meeting_no_help
You head to the nearest village with them. Mabel's lantern lights the road before you as their argument changes to whether the coming winter will be worse than usual. #line:meeting_walk
<<jump briarwood_arrival>>
===
